      <p class="msc-section-kicker">Bitcoin Ecosystem</p>
      <h1>How Bitcoin Communities Form and Grow</h1>
      <p class="msc-learn-page__deck">Bitcoin communities form when people repeatedly learn, build, trade, organize, or solve local problems together. They may gather around software, education, meetups, merchants, policy, art, mining, or payments, but no single group speaks for Bitcoin.

Healthy growth depends less on audience size than on shared practice, clear boundaries, useful work, newcomer pathways, and the ability to handle disagreement without confusing social influence with protocol authority.</p>
