    <section class="msc-learn-key-terms" aria-labelledby="MscGuide078Terms"><h2 id="MscGuide078Terms">Key Terms</h2><dl><div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Bitcoin community</dt><dd>A recurring network of people who learn, coordinate, or work together around Bitcoin.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Community of practice</dt><dd>People who share a domain and improve a practice through repeated interaction.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Domain</dt><dd>The shared subject, problem, or activity that gives a community focus.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Shared practice</dt><dd>The tools, habits, documents, stories, and methods a group develops through participation.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Newcomer pathway</dt><dd>A structured way for a new participant to observe, learn, and contribute.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Peripheral participation</dt><dd>Early participation through observation or limited tasks before taking on deeper responsibility.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Organizer</dt><dd>A person who coordinates meetings, communication, resources, or operations for a group.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Moderator</dt><dd>A person or process that applies participation and conduct rules in a communication space.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Community archive</dt><dd>Durable records such as repositories, meeting notes, mailing-list discussions, and documentation.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Circular Bitcoin economy</dt><dd>A local network in which participants earn and spend bitcoin for goods or services.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Merchant onboarding</dt><dd>Helping a merchant understand, configure, and support Bitcoin payments.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Mentorship</dt><dd>Guidance from a more experienced participant to someone developing skills or context.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Grant program</dt><dd>An organization or process that funds selected contributors or projects.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Sponsor capture</dt><dd>Influence over a group’s agenda or access created by financial dependence.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Gatekeeping</dt><dd>Formal or informal barriers that prevent participation or access to knowledge.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Personality capture</dt><dd>Dependence on a prominent individual whose identity becomes fused with the community.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Platform capture</dt><dd>Dependence on one company or communication system for access, identity, or records.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Information cascade</dt><dd>Acceptance of a claim because others repeat or endorse it rather than because it was independently verified.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Substantiated dissent</dt><dd>A documented objection supported by reasoning or evidence.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Continuity</dt><dd>The ability of a community to keep functioning when organizers, sponsors, tools, or channels change.</dd></div></dl></section>
